  "body": "Found by mkinney's QA runs (p02, p03, p04, p05, p08) and reproduced on a minimal part by a separate verification run on 2026-11-18, CamCraft main `83867fd7` (= v0.24.0 code). Minimal repro projects and posted programs are kept on mkinney's machines and can be attached.\n\nWhat happens: `verify` on a program with tilted operations returns `ok: true` with `gate.not_judged: \"stock sim did not judge this program: SLOT A180: move 2: posed moves are not modelled by the column engine ...\"`, and `post` writes the file. The same slot untilted (`SLOT A0`) is correctly blocked: `move 2 cuts past the finish surface`. The tilted slots cut the same model and post.\n\nWhy P1: an unjudged program must not post as if it were checked (Prime Directive: anything the simulation cannot judge is refused or clearly held, never passed silently).\n\nDone means: either the stock sim judges posed (tilted) moves, or a program it cannot judge is held from posting with a named reason (with an explicit user override if that is the design), pinned by a test with a gouging tilted op that is refused.\n",
